# Repository-tooling conventions
These instructions supplement the root hints whenever Goose reads or changes scripts.

- Scripts must use only the Python standard library and run on Python 3.11+.
- Default to read-only behavior; require an explicit option before modifying files.
- Return a non-zero exit code for validation failures.
- Emit concise, actionable error messages suitable for local use and CI logs.
- Keep these utilities independent of Goose internals; they validate and explain the repository sample only.
